scrcpy (the approach for the helper's Context and Binder handoff)
-----------------------------------------------------------------

The helper runs from app_process as the shell user. It has to make a Context there without calling
LoadedApk.makeApplication, and it has to hand a Binder to the app's content provider from the shell
process. HelperContext.kt, ShellContext.kt and BinderSender.kt (all in
src/main/kotlin/io/github/incallagent/rotep/shell/) follow the approach of the scrcpy server, version
3.3.1: its Workarounds and FakeContext classes (a bare ActivityThread, the system Context wrapped so that
the package name and the attribution source name the shell) and its wrappers ActivityManager and
ContentProvider (getContentProviderExternal, then a call on the provider, then
removeContentProviderExternal).

No scrcpy source file or library is included in the app. The code is written for this app; only the
order of the steps and the idea of the wrapper are taken from scrcpy.

